    I'm sorry about the exclude limit but it is an operating system
limit, not part of the list software. Panix has an old version of DBM
installed which only allows 1024 byte database records. Until a new
DBM library is installed, the limit can't be circumvented without
kludges or a lot of work. Here are some tips to packing more information
into your exclude list.


1) Don't use too many "::exclude thread" or "::exclude user" commands
without arguments or with a message-id. These commands store the entire
subject line as the "pattern" to match.

2) Use partial strings, e.g.
   ::exclude thread guns
      instead of
   ::exclude thread really_long_gun_orientred_subject_line

3) Use regular expressions to do multiuple excludes per command and
wildcards.
   e.g.
   ::exclude guns|rights|environment

4) exclude users using only part of their address, e.g
   ::exclude user foobar@
      instead of
   ::exclude user foobar@foo.bar.baz.edu
    As long as foobar is unique, you won't accidently exclude someone
    by accident.

5) Don't worry if you make a mistake. Any messages accidently filtered
will appear in a daily filterlist sent to you.


Finally, if all else fails, switch to ::exclude all, and INCLUDE those
threads and users you want.

-Ray

