From: rjc@gnu.ai.mit.edu (Ray)
Subject: ADMIN: Auto-nosend

  ::nosend is a command which stores the incoming message to the weekly
cache but does not send it to the list. Since some people have talked
about wanting long messages automatically blocked, I added auto-nosend.
If a message is longer than a certain limit(in this case, 20k), the 
software will post the first 25 lines and a comment on how long the
original message was and how to retrieve it.

  In the future, ::exclude size will be added to allow users to individually
set limits on the sizes of messages they want. However, the global limit
will s till be in place (but raised to a much larger size) just
for preventing of spamming. 

  Finally, there has always been a maximum message size. The list
software will refuse to send any messages larger than this limit.
That's why digests can only be a certain size and why you can't
do ::resend thread .* (retrieve everything!). The current limit is
100k. Most mailers can handle 50k, almost all can handle 100k, but I don't
want to hance anything larger.


